WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.432 --> 00:00:11.355
This is the story of Amelia Earhart.

2
00:00:12.035 --> 00:00:15.236
She was an airplane pilot and a great American hero.

3
00:00:15.956 --> 00:00:23.698
On July 2, 1937, the airplane that Amelia Earhart was flying crashed near Howland Island in the Pacific

4
00:00:23.798 --> 00:00:29.760
Ocean. For many months people searched for Amelia Earhart's plane, but it was never found.

5
00:00:31.412 --> 00:00:38.096
Since 1937 there have been many other expeditions to find Amelia's plane, but no one has been able

6
00:00:38.136 --> 00:00:38.816
to find it.

7
00:00:39.777 --> 00:00:46.520
Amelia Earhart was born on July 24, 1897, to Amy and Edwin Earhart.

8
00:00:47.261 --> 00:00:51.023
She was born in Kansas City, but lived all over the United States.

9
00:00:51.763 --> 00:00:54.465
When she was ten, her family moved to Iowa.

10
00:00:55.205 --> 00:00:57.066
Amelia began keeping a diary.

11
00:00:58.587 --> 00:01:01.848
July 1908: "Today is my tenth birthday.

12
00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:03.409
It was a great day.

13
00:01:04.109 --> 00:01:06.250
Father took us to the Iowa State Fair.

14
00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.130
It was very exciting.

15
00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:10.871
I saw an airplane for the first time.

16
00:01:11.631 --> 00:01:15.832
It was a strange-looking thing, and I can't imagine anyone flying in it."

17
00:01:19.153 --> 00:01:25.275
In 1917, during World War I, Amelia went to visit her sister at school in Canada.

18
00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:28.876
While she was there, she decided to train as a nurse.

19
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:35.964
She served as a volunteer at a military hospital in Toronto and helped heal many soldiers until the

20
00:01:35.984 --> 00:01:37.764
war ended in 1918.

21
00:01:39.645 --> 00:01:46.129
November 1918: "The war has finally ended, and I am going back to the United States.

22
00:01:46.809 --> 00:01:48.150
It was a terrible war.

23
00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:52.652
I tried to help as many soldiers as I could, but many men died.

24
00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.674
I hope there is never another war."

25
00:01:56.494 --> 00:02:00.937
After the war Amelia went to California to be with her mother and father.

26
00:02:01.597 --> 00:02:05.318
It was in California that Amelia fell in love with flying.

27
00:02:07.299 --> 00:02:13.282
December 1920: "A few days ago, I had the most exhilarating day of my life.

28
00:02:14.082 --> 00:02:16.043
I went with Father to Daugherty Field.

29
00:02:16.643 --> 00:02:17.863
We watched an air show.

30
00:02:18.544 --> 00:02:22.465
Today I got a chance to fly in an airplane, and I loved it!

31
00:02:23.106 --> 00:02:24.366
I have to fly again."

32
00:02:25.246 --> 00:02:26.767
January 1921: "I met Neta today.

33
00:02:29.492 --> 00:02:31.594
She is going to give me flying lessons.

34
00:02:32.395 --> 00:02:34.917
I am going to become an airplane pilot!"

35
00:02:36.438 --> 00:02:40.281
March 1921: "This was the worst day of my life.

36
00:02:41.342 --> 00:02:43.363
I had another accident in my airplane.

37
00:02:44.484 --> 00:02:46.946
Neta thinks that I may never be a good pilot.

38
00:02:48.147 --> 00:02:51.210
Mother and Father agree with her and want me to stop flying.

39
00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:53.151
But I will never stop.

40
00:02:54.012 --> 00:02:55.273
Flying is my life now.

41
00:02:55.293 --> 00:02:58.596
I will show them that I can be a great pilot.

42
00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.761
I will become the best pilot ever."

43
00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:08.065
June 1921: "Today I bought an airplane and named it the Canary.

44
00:03:08.725 --> 00:03:12.848
Unfortunately I got into a very small accident when I was landing the plane.

45
00:03:13.628 --> 00:03:14.989
But tomorrow will be better."

46
00:03:15.889 --> 00:03:17.290
Amelia never gave up.

47
00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.513
She worked very hard for the next seven years and became an excellent pilot.

48
00:03:23.233 --> 00:03:26.215
During those seven years, she also became famous.

49
00:03:27.136 --> 00:03:32.017
In fact, the Boston Globe called her the best woman pilot in the United States.

50
00:03:35.638 --> 00:03:39.019
April 1928: "I am so excited.

51
00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.840
Today I got a call from Captain Railey.

52
00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:46.721
He asked me to become the first woman to fly across the Atlantic Ocean.

53
00:03:47.702 --> 00:03:50.883
I will be the captain of the flight, and two men will come with me.

54
00:03:51.823 --> 00:03:55.464
But my dream is to fly across the Atlantic Ocean by myself.”

55
00:03:58.212 --> 00:04:00.874
May 1932: "I did it!

56
00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:03.856
I flew across the Atlantic by myself.

57
00:04:04.517 --> 00:04:06.418
It was not easy, but I persisted.

58
00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:09.460
I encountered a thunderstorm and heavy fog.

59
00:04:10.161 --> 00:04:13.343
All I had to eat on the trip was two cans of tomato juice.

60
00:04:14.103 --> 00:04:19.207
I had hoped to land in Paris, France, but because of the storm, I landed in Ireland."

61
00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:23.750
June 1932: "What a day!

62
00:04:26.676 --> 00:04:29.317
First, there was a parade for me in New York City.

63
00:04:30.077 --> 00:04:33.239
Thousands of people came out onto the street to cheer for me.

64
00:04:34.099 --> 00:04:35.580
I felt like a hero.

65
00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:40.402
Later I flew to Washington DC and went to the White House.

66
00:04:41.262 --> 00:04:43.823
President Hoover presented me with an award."

67
00:04:44.763 --> 00:04:48.625
After her solo Atlantic flight, Amelia was very famous.

68
00:04:49.465 --> 00:04:51.806
Her next goal was to fly around the world.

69
00:04:54.387 --> 00:04:59.713
December 1936: "I have decided to fly all the way around the world.

70
00:05:00.573 --> 00:05:02.193
I will be the first woman to do it.

71
00:05:02.974 --> 00:05:07.375
But even more important, I will fly around the world at the equator.

72
00:05:08.175 --> 00:05:13.296
If I succeed, it will be the longest distance ever traveled in one airplane trip.

73
00:05:14.017 --> 00:05:16.397
Not even any man has flown so far.

74
00:05:17.057 --> 00:05:19.798
The trip will need careful planning and preparation.

75
00:05:20.598 --> 00:05:25.900
I will have to do a trial flight to test equipment, and I'll have to carefully research the

76
00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:26.620
best route."

77
00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:35.946
May 1937: "I said good-bye to my friends, my family, and many of my new fans today.

78
00:05:36.686 --> 00:05:39.228
I have begun my journey around the world.

79
00:05:39.849 --> 00:05:40.950
It will take about a month.

80
00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:46.654
Today I flew from California and I will land in Florida in a few days."

81
00:05:47.555 --> 00:05:51.198
During her long trip, Amelia continued writing her diary.

82
00:05:51.859 --> 00:05:58.304
Whenever she landed, she found a way to send her diary entries home to her husband, George Putnam.

83
00:05:59.884 --> 00:06:02.706
Her last entry was in July 1937.

84
00:06:03.506 --> 00:06:04.487
It was very short.

85
00:06:04.507 --> 00:06:08.089
"Tomorrow I will be flying over Howland Island.

86
00:06:09.109 --> 00:06:10.410
I hope it is a nice day."

87
00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:15.313
Then, the very next day, her plane crashed near Howland Island.

88
00:06:16.053 --> 00:06:18.454
Immediately searchers went out to find her.

89
00:06:19.195 --> 00:06:23.777
President Roosevelt sent 9 Navy ships and 66 airplanes.

90
00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:28.540
They searched for almost a month, but could not find her.

91
00:06:29.404 --> 00:06:33.085
Still to this day, no one has been able to find her plane.

92
00:06:33.965 --> 00:06:37.347
Amelia Earhart was a courageous and brave woman.

93
00:06:38.147 --> 00:06:46.109
Before she left on her flight around the world, Amelia wrote this letter to her husband: Dear George,

94
00:06:46.409 --> 00:06:50.951
Please know I am aware that this trip will be dangerous, but I must make it.

95
00:06:51.791 --> 00:06:54.612
Women must try to do the things that men have done.

96
00:06:55.532 --> 00:07:00.217
Even if I fail, I hope that my adventure will challenge other women to try.
